        "title": "06 · Hand back the result",
        "phase": "output",
        "instruction": "ONLY after the owner has said yes, hand the result back as a Result card they can paste into this graph. First write one plain sentence: copy the block below, click the empty canvas of this graph in Twilite, and paste (Ctrl+V, or Cmd+V on a Mac); it appears as a card named Result. Then give ONE fenced json block of exactly this shape: {\"action\":\"createNodes\",\"nodes\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Result · <runId>\",\"position\":{\"x\":0,\"y\":0},\"width\":560,\"height\":430,\"data\":{\"content\":{\"kind\":\"markdown\",\"value\":\"<the card text>\"},\"result\":<the approved answer JSON, exactly as approved>}}]}. The card text is short and readable: a heading with the runId, the line \"answerStatus: resolved\" (or unresolved or blocked), a table of sku, available, shortfall, packs and orderUnits for each order, and the two totals. Write it as one JSON string with \\n for line breaks. If your environment can place nodes in the open editor, offer to place the card for the owner instead of making them paste. After the block, report the two outcomes separately: the answer (answerStatus, with the evidence satisfied and missing) and the procedure (each stage and whether it passed). State what was not done: nothing was saved, written or purchased, and the card is only in the graph the owner pastes it into. Say whether the preflight was actually invoked. If the owner wants a change, go back to stage 04. If the owner declines, hand back nothing and say so.",
        "inputs": "verifiedCandidate\nownerApproval\nrunId",
        "outputs": "resultCard\nreport",
